# ParcelTrack.http: requests you send with one click.
# In Visual Studio (or VS Code with the REST Client extension), open this file and click
# "Send request" above a request.
#
# @host is the address in your browser when you press F5 (the http profile).
@host = http://localhost:5420

# Paste the token from request 3 here (the value of "token" in the JSON reply, with no
# quotes). # @name request variables that take the token from the login reply are also
# allowed, in place of pasting.
@staff_token = PASTE_THE_STAFF_TOKEN_HERE

# Paste the token from request 9 here (the admin token).
@admin_token = PASTE_THE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

# A program says which one it is on every write. The branch desk program sends this.
@client = Branch desk


### 1. GET /api/parcels - every parcel. Expect 200 OK with a JSON list, each with a deliveryFee
# (the seeded fees are 800, 650, 1250, 2000, 1250 for parcels 1 to 5).
GET {{host}}/api/parcels


### 2. POST /api/parcels with NO token - the write is locked. Expect 401 Unauthorized
# (never a 302 to the login page). Nothing is added.
POST {{host}}/api/parcels
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client: {{client}}

{
  "trackingCode": "PT-200201",
  "recipient": "Damion Clarke",
  "weightKg": 4.2,
  "status": "Received",
  "branchId": 5
}


### 3. POST /api/auth/login as staff@parceltrack.test - right password. Expect 200 OK and a
# token that lasts 60 minutes. Copy the "token" value from the reply into @staff_token above.
# @name staffLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff@parceltrack.test",
  "password": "Pass123!"
}


### 4. POST /api/auth/login as staff@parceltrack.test - WRONG password. Expect 401 Unauthorized,
# with the same message as an unknown email.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "staff@parceltrack.test",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}


### 5. Request 2 again, WITH the Staff token and an X-Client header. Expect 201 Created with a
# Location header pointing at the new parcel.
POST {{host}}/api/parcels
Authorization: Bearer {{staff_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client: {{client}}

{
  "trackingCode": "PT-200201",
  "recipient": "Damion Clarke",
  "weightKg": 4.2,
  "status": "Received",
  "branchId": 5
}


### 6. POST with the Staff token, tracking code AB-12 (wrong format). Expect 400 Bad Request
# with the Part E message: "Tracking code must look like PT-123456". Nothing is added.
POST {{host}}/api/parcels
Authorization: Bearer {{staff_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client: {{client}}

{
  "trackingCode": "AB-12",
  "recipient": "Bad Code",
  "weightKg": 1.0,
  "status": "Received",
  "branchId": 1
}


### 7. POST with the Staff token, NO X-Client header. Expect 400 Bad Request with the Part C
# message: "Say which program is calling: add an X-Client header". The action does not run,
# so nothing is added.
POST {{host}}/api/parcels
Authorization: Bearer {{staff_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingCode": "PT-200202",
  "recipient": "Nadine Walker",
  "weightKg": 1.0,
  "status": "Received",
  "branchId": 1
}


### 8. DELETE /api/parcels/5 with the Staff token. Staff may not delete. Expect 403 Forbidden.
DELETE {{host}}/api/parcels/5
Authorization: Bearer {{staff_token}}
X-Client: {{client}}


### 9. POST /api/auth/login as admin@parceltrack.test - right password. Expect 200 OK and a
# token that lasts 60 minutes. Copy the "token" value from the reply into @admin_token above.
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@parceltrack.test",
  "password": "Pass123!"
}


### 10. DELETE /api/parcels/5 with the Admin token. Expect 204 No Content.
DELETE {{host}}/api/parcels/5
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_token}}
X-Client: {{client}}
